id: pm-jev-6fs0
title: Update triage and link backlog tests for typed host lookup refusals on the pinned toolchain
description: "The pm-toolchain Dependabot bump pins @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.28, whose GH-1613 change preserves typed PmClient lookup refusals: reading or mutating an item whose document is missing from disk now fails with the host code item_not_found instead of an unclassified error. The batch triage and link backlog tests asserted the old generic fallback reasons (jev_triage_failure, jev_link_failure); the host-error retention they guard (outcome failed, exit code 1, no receipts applied) is unchanged, and the rows now carry the more precise host code."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: dependencies,"gh:unbraind/pm-jev#75",migration,sdk
created_at: "2026-11-03T09:59:09.226Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T00:45:56.153Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-04T00:45:56.127Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-04T00:45:56.127Z"
author: pi-toolchain-glm-1103
resolution: Implemented and merged in #75 (8ee4d7f).
expected_result: The change described by this item is on main.
actual_result: "Merged in #75 as 8ee4d7f; checks successful at head 658428c: CodeQL, codeql, enable-auto-merge, test (22), test (26)."
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-03T09:59:26.357Z",pi-toolchain-glm-1103,"Reproduced both failures locally: test/batch-triage.test.ts 'deleted and missing source documents...' expects jev_triage_failure for the missing-file case and test/link.test.ts 'link backlog preserves missing-source host failures...' expects jev_link_failure; both rows now report the host code item_not_found. Root cause: pm-cli 2026.10.28 GH-1613 preserves typed PmClient lookup refusals, so a missing item document surfaces item_not_found through the pm-jev error mapping instead of falling back to the generic decision-failure codes. Classification: test pinned old CLI behaviour; production code is correct (the host error is retained, receipts are not applied, exit code stays 1). Fix: assert item_not_found for the missing-document cases and document the upstream reference in a comment; keep every other assertion."
  "2026-11-03T10:27:13.958Z",pi-toolchain-glm-1103,"Evidence: node --test test/batch-triage.test.ts test/link.test.ts passes 28/28 (both previously failing tests included). Full suite npm test passes 398/398, plus typecheck and lint green. The merge from main took main's lockfile and @types/node 26.6.6 and kept the PR's pinned toolchain (@unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.28, pm-changelog 2026.10.28, pm-ops 2026.10.29), re-resolved with a package-lock-only install. No production change was needed; the new typed refusal codes are an upstream improvement, recorded here for the review."
  "2026-11-03T12:22:03.288Z",grok-jev-coverage-1103,"Coverage follow-up on the toolchain PR: CI passes 398 tests but branch coverage is 99.75% because index.ts fallbacks jev_triage_failure and jev_link_failure are no longer reached after the typed item_not_found contract. Plan: keep both item_not_found assertions, add untyped plain-Error decision failures that assert those exact fallback reasons with no receipt and unchanged exit codes, rename the link test so its name matches the typed contract, prove each new case fails if the ?? fallback is replaced with mapped.code, then restore and run the full gate."
  "2026-11-03T12:35:59.037Z",grok-jev-coverage-1103,"Coverage restoration: a plain Error is mapped by translateDecisionError to jev_malformed_answer, so it cannot reach the nullish fallback. The reachable untyped decision failure is the existing code-less model-replacement refusal (expected error, no context.code), driven through the fake decision server. New tests keep the item_not_found assertions and assert failed rows, exact fallback reasons, no receipts, and exit code 1. Link missing-source test renamed to match item_not_found. Mutation proof: replacing each ?? fallback with mapped.code makes that new test fail (reason undefined versus jev_triage_failure or jev_link_failure); both lines restored. No production hook added."
  "2026-11-03T13:08:41.735Z",grok-jev-coverage-1103,"Gates: npm run coverage passed 400/400 with 100% statements, branches, functions and lines, including index.ts. npm run lint, npm run typecheck, npm run duplication and changelog:check passed after regenerating the unreleased changelog section. npm test was not repeated separately; the coverage command already executed the full suite under the branch gate."
  "2026-11-03T13:22:40.762Z",claude-orchestrator,"Coverage round (CI on a37d005: index.ts branches 99.75%, lines 1552/1868). The GH-1613 test update left the generic fallback reasons unreached. Grok's agent (credits ran out before it committed) and the orchestrator added serveDigestReplacement: a digest-bound calibration whose model digest changes after the first decision, so calibrated inference throws an expected error with no context.code (a plain transport Error maps to jev_malformed_answer instead). New tests: batch triage keeps a failed row with jev_triage_failure, link backlog with jev_link_failure; no receipts, exit 1. Mutation: dropping either ?? fallback fails its test 0/1. npm run coverage 400/400, index.ts 100/100/100; lint, typecheck, changelog:check pass."
